Vogel opposed new restrictions on guns, while Fairfax called for universal background checks. Vogel said she opposed changing Virginia's no-limits campaign finance rules, saying caps would restrict speech. Fairfax noted a $600,000 donation Vogel received from a relative. That relative was her father, William Holtzman, founder of Holtzman Oil. Fairfax said he supports limits so that wealthy interests "do not drown out other people's voices."
